// macroman.cla: emitui golden fixture -- pins MacRoman source-byte
// pass-through (docs/clarus-language-reference.md's "Source encoding"
// section, Chapter 2): .cla source files are MacRoman, not UTF-8, so a
// menu caption containing the MacRoman ellipsis glyph (byte 0xC9) and an
// alert string containing MacRoman curly quotes (bytes 0xD2/0xD3) must
// reach the emitted C's string literals as the identical raw bytes,
// verbatim -- no re-encoding. Modeled on the real-world bug this pins:
// examples/texteditor.cla's menu captions and alert once carried UTF-8
// typographic bytes instead (mac-target-4c Fix 2).

menu File {
    item Open "Open…" key "O"
}

on App.launch {
    alert("Saved “ok”")
}
